law firm. These initial consultations with our attorneys are always offered at no cost and with absolutely no risk to our prospective clients. ","imageId":0,"imageUrl":"","imageFallback":"img-team.png","imageAlt":"Hastings and Hastings legal team"}],"howWeHelpIntro":"In the moments immediately following an accident, your legal options likely aren't the first thing on your mind, and for obvious reasons. Instead, you're likely thinking of the most important things – the safety and well-being of yourself and your loved ones. But in the days, months, and weeks following an accident, you will likely quickly realize that the accident's aftereffects are much larger than you might have planned for.","howWeHelpItems":[{"text":"Accidents are expensive. In obtaining medical treatment, victims rack up significant expenses in hospital bills, insurance copays, medication, transportation, and doctor office visits. Additionally, many victims are unable to work, leading to lost wages and in some cases, loss of employment entirely. Victims may have suffered property damage, even damage and injury from riding a bicycle as well as in the form of a totaled car, damage to their home, or loss of belongings. Some medical emergency may include loss of limbs, which is where the best Mesa amputation injury lawyer will be the main point of contact.","imageId":0,"imageUrl":"","imageFallback":"accident-ambulance.jpg","imageAlt":"Multi-vehicle accident scene with ambulance at night","imagePosition":"left"},{"text":"Long story short, accidents are incredibly expensive for victims. Lawsuits allow victims to recover the money they've lost due to the negligence or carelessness of another person or company. A personal injury lawyer's entire purpose is assisting victims in accessing the funds to which they are legally entitled, so a victim is fully and fairly compensated for the injuries they have suffered.","imageId":0,"imageUrl":"","imageFallback":"billing-statement.jpg","imageAlt":"Medical billing statement with stethoscope","imagePosition":"right"}],"caseCategoriesClosing":"In addition to these types of cases, our team is willing to consider any type of personal injury lawsuit. Since we have some of the best weather and beautiful lakes, we also offer the <a href="/mesa-boat-accident-attorney/">best Mesa Boat accident attorney in the area</a>. In other words, if you have found yourself injured due to the wrongful acts or omissions of another person, company, or group of people, we want to hear from you. Our free consultations are offered at no cost and no risk to prospective clients, and our team is ready to listen to your story.","testimonials":[{"quote":"Hastings and Hastings handled my claim after I had tried to deal with insurance company myself.","authorName":"Verified Client","authorRole":"Car Accident Victim","rating":5},{"quote":"I was in a car accident a few months ago and could not be happier with the outcome. Sean Hennick, my attorney, along with all the other staff at Hastings and Hastings, were extremely professional and helpful. Having Hastings and Hastings by my side made this process seem easy. I would highly recommend Hastings and Hastings to anyone I know.","authorName":"Verified Client","authorRole":"Car Accident Victim","rating":5},{"quote":"They are great! They do preliminary questions to make sure that you aren't wasting your time (or theirs). They stand up for you and do what is right for you. Can't say enough positive comments on how they handled my case. They are responsive to emails and follow up. They only take legitimate cases and don't subscribe to "frivolous" lawsuits.","authorName":"Verified Client","authorRole":"Injury Victim","rating":4},{"quote":"I can't say how happy I am with Hastings & Hastings right now. I came to them about 9 months ago after my accident and today I received my settlement. Everyone there was very nice and helpful. My attorney's paralegal always responded to my emails quickly which really impressed me. I'm so pleased with my experience with them that I had to write a review!","authorName":"Verified Client","authorRole":"Accident Victim","rating":5}],"faqItems":[{"question":"Q. How Do I Know If I Have a Personal Injury Case?","answer":"<p>To determine if you have a personal injury case, consider the following factors:<br><strong>Injury or Harm:</strong> You must have suffered physical, emotional, or financial harm due to the actions or negligence of another party. This harm could result from accidents, intentional acts, or even defective products.<br><strong>Fault or Negligence:</strong> You need to establish that someone else's actions or negligence caused or contributed to your injury. Negligence refers to a failure to exercise reasonable care, leading to harm to others.<br><strong>Duty of Care:</strong> The at-fault party must have owed you a duty of care. For example, in a car accident, drivers have a duty to follow traffic rules and drive safely.<br><strong>Breach of Duty:</strong> You must show that the at-fault party breached their duty of care. In other words, they failed to act in a manner expected under the circumstances.<br><strong>Causation:</strong> You need to demonstrate a direct link between the at-fault party's breach of duty and your injury. The breach must be the cause of your harm.<br><strong>Damages:</strong> You must have suffered quantifiable damages due to the injury, such as medical expenses, lost wages, pain and suffering, or property damage.<br><strong>Time Limit:</strong> Personal injury cases have a statute of limitations, which is the time frame within which you must file your claim. In Arizona, this time limit can vary depending on the type of case.<br>If you believe that the above criteria apply to your situation, it's essential to consult with a qualified personal injury attorney. They can evaluate the details of your case, assess its strengths and weaknesses, and advise you on the best course of action. Personal injury attorneys are experienced in handling such cases and can guide you through the legal process to pursue the compensation you may be entitled to for your injuries and losses. Keep in mind that each case is unique, so seeking professional legal advice is crucial to understanding your specific circumstances.</p>","isOpen":false},{"question":"Q. Will My Personal Injury Case Be Settled Out of Court?","answer":"<p>Most personal injury cases in Arizona are settled out of court. However, the specific outcome depends on the facts and circumstances of each case. Our attorneys are prepared to take your case to trial if a fair settlement cannot be reached.</p>","isOpen":false},{"question":"Q. What Evidence Will I Need For My Mesa Personal Injury Lawyer?","answer":"<p>Important evidence includes medical records, photographs of the accident scene and injuries, witness statements, police reports, and documentation of lost wages and expenses. Your attorney will help gather and preserve evidence on your behalf.</p>","isOpen":false}]} /-->

